    "description": "Live Oak Wind Farm is an operating onshore wind project in Texas. Its end markets are wholesale and contracted power offtake, with public materials indicating that the project sells renewable generation into the Texas market. The project is asset-heavy and based on operating wind generation infrastructure rather than providing development services only. Public sources describe the facility as roughly 200 MW and note that it uses 76 Siemens Gamesa turbines in Schleicher County near San Angelo. Reviewed sources did not disclose current project revenue, merchant exposure, or the economic split within John Laing Investments Limited. The asset is associated in the master workbook with John Laing Investments Limited, the holding structure backed by Equitix and KKR, and public materials state that the project became operational in 2018.",
